---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

// The canonical Creator Store identity for the plugin, "StudPilot Studio". The asset id has exactly ONE definition in this repository
// (packages/shared/src/index.ts) and everything, including this page, derives from it. Do not restate the number here; a second copy is a second
// thing to forget to change.
import {
  STUDIO_PLUGIN_ASSET_ID as ASSET_ID,
  STUDIO_PLUGIN_URL as STORE_URL,
  STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE as storeLive,
  STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_REFUSAL as refusal,
} from '../../lib/studio-plugin';

/*
 * THE PLUGIN PAGE, REWRITTEN (M2 site fix cycle 1, plan step 2.6): AVAILABILITY FROM THE FLAG, and the three pages that were about the same
 * plugin folded into it. /docs/connect (pairing, in Getting started), /docs/updating (the "Updating" section below) and /docs/build-from-source
 * (a developer path that was explicitly not how anyone installs StudPilot; deleted, and redirected here) are Astro redirects now.
 *
 * `storeLive` decides whether this page is an install guide or an availability notice, and it decides the metadata too: a description is what a
 * search result and a pasted link show, so it must never promise an install path the body denies (tests/plugin-availability-metadata.test.mjs).
 * While STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE is false new customers cannot get the plugin: the page says so first and says what still works.
 *
 * `refusal` is kept for the day a listing is refused again: while one is recorded, the page states Roblox's own reason rather than only the
 * outcome (tests/plugin-listing-identity.test.mjs). It is null from 2026-09-22, when the listing was distributed again.
 *
 * What the plugin can and cannot do is the plugin's own sentence (apps/studpilot-plugin/src/init.server.luau, the disclosure under "Enable
 * edits…"), quoted, and tests/docs-plugin-claims.test.mjs holds it to that file.
 */
const decided = refusal
  ? new Date(refusal.decidedAt).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' })
  : null;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="The Studio plugin | StudPilot"
  description={storeLive
    ? 'The free StudPilot Studio plugin: how to get it from the Roblox Creator Store, what it can and cannot do, how to pair it and how to update it.'
    : 'Public Studio installation is unavailable right now. What that means, what still works, what the plugin does and how to update it if you already have it.'}
  heading="The Studio plugin"
  order={2}
  summary="Whether you can get the plugin today, what it does, and how to update it."
>
  <p>
    <strong>StudPilot Studio</strong> is the plugin that lets StudPilot reach the place you have open in Roblox Studio. Without it the web app can
    chat and plan with you. With it paired, and edits allowed, StudPilot can change that one place.
  </p>

  {
    storeLive ? (
      <p>
        <a href={STORE_URL} class="btn btn-primary" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Get StudPilot Studio on the Creator Store <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>{' '}
        It is free. The link opens Roblox's site in a new tab.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <div class="callout">
        {
          refusal ? (
            <p>
              <strong>Public installation is unavailable, and it is a moderation decision.</strong> Roblox removed this plugin's Creator Store
              listing (<code>{ASSET_ID}</code>) on {decided}, giving the reason <strong>“{refusal.reason}”</strong>, so the store URL is not a
              working install path.
              {refusal.appealId ? ' An appeal has been sent and is awaiting a decision.' : ' An appeal has not been sent.'}{' '}
              New customers can chat and plan in the web app, and cannot build in Studio yet.
            </p>
          ) : (
            <p>
              <strong>Public installation is unavailable right now.</strong> The plugin (<code>{ASSET_ID}</code>) cannot be installed from the
              Creator Store today, so new customers can chat and plan in the web app and cannot build in Studio yet. The status page lists it as a
              known issue. If you already have the plugin, it may still work.
            </p>
          )
        }
      </div>
    )
  }

  <h2>{storeLive ? 'Getting it' : 'When installation opens again'}</h2>
  <p>
    Roblox splits installation into two halves, and the second half happens inside Studio: a web page cannot install a plugin into Studio. You get
    the plugin from the Creator Store page, then install it from Studio's <strong>Toolbox</strong>, under <strong>Inventory</strong>. A
    <strong>StudPilot</strong> button then appears in the <strong>Plugins</strong> tab. If it does not, open <strong>Manage Plugins</strong> and
    switch the plugin on.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first time it talks to StudPilot, Studio can ask you to allow the plugin to reach the network. Allow it, or the panel says
    “Could not reach StudPilot”. You can accept, deny or revoke that in Studio's plugin management window.
  </p>

  <h2>Pairing, and what you allow</h2>
  <p>
    The plugin does nothing until you pair it with a project by typing a six-character code, and it starts with edits off. Pairing, the code and
    turning edits on are in <a href="/docs/getting-started#pair">Getting started</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What it can and cannot do</h2>
  <p>
    This is the plugin's own wording from the panel, under <strong>Enable edits…</strong>: StudPilot may create or change supported objects and
    scripts in the place you paired, control a Run-mode playtest, and start a short Test session with a player. It cannot publish, upload assets or
    execute arbitrary received Luau inside the plugin. Writes need edit mode, and the plugin opens an undo recording for each. Disconnecting turns
    the permission off. It works only while Studio is open with that place.
  </p>

  <h2 id="updating">Updating</h2>
  <p>
    Roblox does not update Studio plugins on its own. In Studio open <strong>Plugins</strong>, then <strong>Manage Plugins</strong>, find
    StudPilot and press <strong>Update</strong>. If your build is too old for the server, the panel says so, and builds are blocked until
    you update.
  </p>

  <h2>Removing it</h2>
  <p>
    Uninstall it from Studio's plugin management window, the same place you manage every other plugin. To stop StudPilot acting on a place without
    uninstalling anything, press <strong>Disconnect</strong> in the panel, or disconnect from the project in the web app. If something does not
    line up, <a href="/docs/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a> lists what the panel can say.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
